WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.909
Apples turn brown because of a process called oxidation. This happens

00:00:04.909 --> 00:00:09.818
when the skin of the apple is exposed to oxygen in

00:00:09.818 --> 00:00:14.727
the air. Let's explore this process in more detail. Watch this

00:00:14.727 --> 00:00:18.297
animation to see how it works. Watch animation

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:24.036
Oxidation is a chemical reaction. It happens when an apple's skin

00:00:24.036 --> 00:00:29.422
comes into contact with oxygen. Let's see how this works with

00:00:29.422 --> 00:00:34.807
a labeled diagram. Watch this animation to see the process. Watch

00:00:34.807 --> 00:00:35.297
animation

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:40.153
To prevent apples from turning brown, we can use a few

00:00:40.153 --> 00:00:44.656
simple methods. One is to keep apples in a plastic bag.

00:00:44.656 --> 00:00:49.158
This traps the moisture inside and slows down the oxidation process.

